# NEXUS — Cursor / AI agent rules
# (Full context: docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md, docs/BACKENDS.md, docs/AGENTS.md)

NEXUS is a React+TS+Vite streaming app (rebrand of P-Stream/movie-web).
It scrapes third-party sources via "providers"; metadata comes from TMDB.

RULES:
1. Never reintroduce P-Stream / Z-Stream / pstream / zstream branding.
   Brand logo is public/pwa-logo.svg. App name is NEXUS everywhere.
2. Only WORKING providers may appear in the source list and spinner.
   Always build the list from getLiveNexusProviders()
   (src/providers/nexus-providers-index.ts). Hide dead providers.
3. MovieBox provider is MP4-ONLY. Drop DASH. (Player has no DASH support.)
4. Every provider returns the same shape:
   { embeds: [], stream: { id, type, playlist, flags, captions, qualities?, audioTracks? } }
5. Original audio is the default track. Dub languages (MovieBox) are opt-in
   via the player Audio menu (AudioTrackSelector.tsx + utils/player/audioTracks.ts).
6. Secrets live ONLY in .env (VITE_-prefixed). Never hardcode tokens/URLs.

BACKENDS:
- enc-dec.app: decrypts VidLink/Videasy/VidFast/Hexa/yFlix payloads.
- TMDB-Embed (HuggingFace): VITE_TMDB_EMBED_API_URL, provider rank 900.
- MovieBox (VPS FastAPI): VITE_MOVIEBOX_API_URL, slug-based, multi-audio dubs.

DEBUG PLAYBACK (in order): .env correctness → provider health →
MovieBox audio field (adjust strategy A/B/C in moviebox-provider.ts,
see BACKENDS.md §3.4) → CORS (set proxy env vars).

COMMANDS: pnpm install; pnpm run dev (5173); pnpm run build; pnpm run preview.
